Description: A systematic bibliometric pipeline for mapping occupational risk
    evidence in any domain - emerging technologies, established hazards, or
    specific industrial sectors. ORISMA automates the full workflow from
    multi-database ingestion (RIS, BibTeX, CSV) through automatic deduplication,
    risk category extraction via a normative dictionary (ISO 45001 / INSST /
    NIOSH), co-occurrence analysis, hierarchical clustering, and generation of
    three original indicators: the Worker-Risk Disconnection Index (WRDI), the
    Risk Category Saturation Index (RCS), and the Material-Gap Profile (MGP).
    Outputs include structured data files, publication-ready visualizations,
    bilingual executive reports (English/Spanish), PRISMA-compliant logs, and
    reproducibility certificates. Designed for occupational health researchers
    and safety practitioners with minimal R experience.
